    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UAF_External_Career_Site/job/Fayetteville-AR/Teaching-Assistant-Professor_R0090589": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students.” University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Student Jobs at UAF.” All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 09/29/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation’s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation’s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli­cants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Accounting Department's Website: https://walton.uark.edu/departments/accounting/ Summary of Job Duties: The William Dillard Department of Accounting in the Sam M. Walton College of Business at the University of Arkansas seeks applications from interested candidates to fill a non-tenure track Teaching Assistant Professor position effective August 16, 2027. A Teaching Assistant Professor is expected to teach eight courses per year with a mix of face-to-face and online courses, as needed. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience; benefits are competitive. Regular on-campus availability, in-person teaching, and active contribution to the life of the department, including exhibiting respect and cooperation in shared academic and administrative tasks are essential duties. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications:   Hold a Ph.D. with an emphasis in accounting from a nationally or internationally accredited university Evidence of high-quality teaching in undergraduate and/or graduate accounting courses Evidence or potential to provide both face-to-face and online undergraduate and/or graduate accounting courses Must meet standards to be classified as Scholarly Academic under AACSB (this could include recent publications in peer-reviewed journals and/or engagement in professional practice through outreach, consulting, or other activities consistent with AACSB standards.) Preferred Qualifications:   Experience teaching courses focused on individual and/or corporate taxation Evidence or potential to publish in peer-reviewed accounting journals with a primary research emphasis in tax accounting Additional Information: The William Dillard Department of Accounting: The department develops outstanding students and faculty who meaningfully impact the global accounting community. The department currently has eleven tenured or tenure-track faculty members, eight teaching/clinical faculty members, two full-time Executive in Residence faculty members, six full-time instructors, and several part-time lecturers. The department offers an undergraduate degree program in accounting and graduate programs at both the master’s and doctoral levels. The department also offers a five-year integrated program, which leads to the simultaneous awarding of an undergraduate degree and a master’s degree. The department’s programs are accredited by the AACSB, which ensures quality and promotes excellence and continuous improvement in undergraduate and graduate education. The department was named as part of a gift provided in honor of William Dillard Sr.    The Sam M. Walton College of Business:  The Sam M. Walton College of Business promotes the values of being “EPIC”, which stands for Excellence, Professionalism, Innovation and Collegiality. The Walton College has nearly 10,000 students. The Walton College has an innovative cross-functional business core program that focuses on business processes, and several new cross-disciplinary minors and concentrations. The Walton College has consistently been ranked among the nation’s top 25 public undergraduate business schools since 2005, according to  U.S. News and World Report .  The University of Arkansas: The flagship campus of the University of Arkansas has a total enrollment of approximately 34,000 students. It recently completed a successful capital campaign that raised about $1.45 billion.  Location : The University of Arkansas is located in Fayetteville, in the Ozark Mountains of Northwest Arkansas. Fayetteville offers a high quality of life, a mild climate, excellent health care, a variety of restaurants, a cost-of-living index of 92.9, and is minutes from lakes and rivers for fishing, swimming, and boating. Fayetteville’s Walton Arts Center and Theatre Squared offer a rich variety of Broadway, symphony, dance, jazz, and other performances and special events. US News consistently ranks Fayetteville among the 10 best places to live in the U.S., with the most recent ranking (2023) of #10. Fayetteville is a city of approximately 85,000 with a regional (Northwest Arkansas) population of about 535,000. Northwest Arkansas has one of the highest growth rates in the U.S. and was ranked 40th among the “best places for Business and Careers” by Forbes in 2023. Several Fortune 500 companies have their headquarters in Northwest Arkansas, including Walmart, Tyson Foods, and J.B. Hunt Transportation.  Check out this site for more information: https://walton.uark.edu/about/ Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae, List of three Professional References (name, email, business title) Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Caleb Rawson Associate Professor of Accounting Sam M. Walton College of Business CRawson@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Job posting will close at 12:01 AM on close date above. Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UAF_External_Career_Site/job/Fayetteville-AR/Research-Associate-or-Full-Professor--open-rank-_R0090652": {
      "title": "Research Associate or Full Professor (open rank)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students.” University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Student Jobs at UAF.” All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 11/01/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Non-Tenure Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Academic Term (Fixed Term) Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation’s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation’s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli­cants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Supply Chain Management Department's Website: Summary of Job Duties: The J.B. Hunt Transport Department of Supply Chain Management in the Sam M. Walton College of Business at the University of Arkansas invites applications and nominations for a non-tenure-track research faculty position in Supply Chain Management, at the rank of Research Associate Professor or Research Professor, beginning August 16, 2027. Rank will be determined by the candidate’s qualifications, experience, accomplishments, and demonstrated impact. This position is part of a coordinated faculty cluster hire in supply chain management focused on contested logistics and defense-relevant supply chain research. The department is concurrently recruiting multiple tenure-track and research faculty whose collective expertise will extend the University of Arkansas’s leadership in contested logistics, military and defense logistics, and national security supply chains, in close partnership with the Contested Logistics Consortium and the Supply Chain Management Research Center (SCMRC). This cluster in contested logistics and supply chain aligns with one of the University’s and College’s key strategic priorities and builds critical mass in a high-importance academic and research domain. It advances the land-grant mission by connecting research, instruction, and outreach to pressing state and societal needs. This position is designed for a scholar-practitioner or research faculty member who can produce industry-relevant, analytically rigorous, and practically actionable research addressing important supply chain challenges facing companies, public-sector organizations, defense stakeholders, and broader society. The successful candidate will focus primarily on industry-engaged research, applied research translation, outreach, research partnership development, and practitioner-facing thought leadership, while contributing to the department and college’s broader research, teaching, and service mission. A central emphasis of this role is research, translation, and engagement that directly supports military and defense logistics stakeholders, including activities associated with the Contested Logistics Consortium and Department of War-related research priorities. The department is especially interested in candidates who can bridge academic research, industry practice, and external engagement. Successful candidates should be capable of developing research outputs that may include practitioner journal articles, white papers, industry reports, research briefs, executive-facing insights, case studies, applied research projects, conference presentations, and, where appropriate, peer-reviewed academic publications. The ideal candidate will have the ability to translate complex research into insights useful to executives, policymakers, supply chain leaders, faculty colleagues, students, and external partners. This role is intentionally focused on industry-facing research and outreach. The successful candidate will help expand the department and Supply Chain Management Research Center’s ability to identify and frame high-value supply chain research questions emerging from industry, government, defense, nonprofit, and public-sector partners, conduct applied research that is rigorous, credible, and useful to supply chain decision makers, translate research into practitioner-oriented publications, executive education content, industry briefings, workshops, and public thought leadership, build sustained relationships with corporate, public-sector, and professional partners, support externally engaged research initiatives that enhance the visibility, relevance, and impact of the department and Walton College, and collaborate with tenure-track faculty, clinical faculty, research center leaders, doctoral students, executives in residence, and external stakeholders. This position is intended to strengthen the department’s capacity for externally engaged research, industry outreach, applied scholarship, and research translation. Regular on-campus availability, in-person teaching, and active contribution to the life of the department, including exhibiting respect and cooperation in shared academic and administrative tasks are essential duties. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree in supply chain management, logistics, operations management, or a closely related field completed by the position start date Demonstrated ability to conduct high-quality research related to supply chain management, logistics, operations, analytics, or a closely related domain U.S. citizenship, due to access to export-controlled information, restricted federal data, and security-sensitive research environments Demonstrated record of developing and securing externally sponsored research funding, or an exceptional record of senior military or defense logistics leadership and accomplishment Preferred Qualifications: Experience leading large-scale research initiatives, external partnerships, outreach programs, or multidisciplinary research efforts Demonstrated record of producing practitioner-oriented research outputs, such as white papers, industry reports, executive briefs, applied research studies, case studies, benchmarking reports, or practitioner journal articles Experience designing and facilitating industry workshops, executive briefings, roundtables, conferences, webinars, or professional education programs Professional experience in supply chain management, logistics, transportation, procurement, retail, manufacturing, defense logistics, public-sector logistics, analytics, consulting, technology, or related fields An active U.S. security clearance, or eligibility to obtain and maintain one Significant military, defense logistics, or national security supply chain experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilitie s (KSAs): Strong written and oral communication skills, including the ability to translate complex ideas for practitioners and executive audiences Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, industry partners, and external stakeholders Ability to collaborate with tenure-track faculty on research projects that may contribute to peer-reviewed academic publications Ability to contribute to the mission of a research-oriented business school and a highly engaged supply chain, business, and university faculty Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position  and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .  Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant’s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Marc Scott Assistant Chair Department of Supply Chain Management MScott@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Deadline is October 31, 2026 at 12:01 AM Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"
    },
    "https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UAF_External_Career_Site/job/Fayetteville-AR/Assistant-Professor_R0090609": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Two Open Positions)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCurrent University of Arkansas System employees, including student employees and graduate assistants, need to log in to Workday via MyApps.Microsoft.com, then access Find Jobs from the Workday search bar to view and apply for open positions. Students at all University of Arkansas institutions will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Jobs for Students.” University of Arkansas, Fayetteville students will view open positions and apply within Workday by searching for “Find Student Jobs at UAF.” All Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). If you close the browser or exit your application prior to submitting, the application process will be saved as a draft. You will be able to access and complete the application through “My Draft Applications” located on your Candidate Home page. Closing Date: 11/01/2026 Type of Position: Faculty - Tenure/Tenure Track Workstudy Position: No Job Type: Regular Work Shift: Sponsorship Available: No Institution Name: University of Arkansas, Fayetteville Founded in 1871, the University of Arkansas is a land grant institution, classified by the Carnegie Foundation among the nation’s top 2 percent of universities with the highest level of research activity. The University of Arkansas works to advance the state and build a better world through education, research, and outreach by providing transformational opportunities and skills, fostering a welcoming climate, and nurturing creativity, discovery, and the spread of new ideas and innovations. The University of Arkansas campus is located in Fayetteville, a welcoming community ranked as one of the best places to live in the U.S. The growing region surrounding Fayetteville is home to numerous Fortune 500 companies and one of the nation’s strongest economies. Northwest Arkansas is also quickly gaining a national reputation for its focus on the arts and overall quality of life. As an employer, the University of Arkansas offers a vibrant work environment and a workplace culture that promotes a healthy work-life balance. The benefits package includes university contributions to health, dental, life and disability insurance, tuition waivers for employees and their families, 12 official holidays, immediate leave accrual, and a choice of retirement programs with university contributions ranging from 5 to 10% of employee salary. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions, you should review before applying for the opening. If you have a disability and need assistance with the hiring process, please submit a request via the Disability Accommodations | OEOC | University of Arkansas (uark.edu) : Request an Accommodation. Appli­cants are required to submit a request for each position of which they have applied. For general application assistance or if you have questions about a job posting, please contact Human Resources at 479.575.5351. Department: Supply Chain Management Department's Website: https://walton.uark.edu/departments/supplychain/ Summary of Job Duties: The J.B. Hunt Transport Department of Supply Chain Management in the Sam M. Walton College of Business at the University of Arkansas invites applications and nominations for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Supply Chain Management, beginning August 16, 2027. These positions are part of a coordinated faculty cluster hire in supply chain management focused on contested logistics and defense-relevant supply chain research. The department is concurrently recruiting multiple tenure-track and research faculty whose collective expertise will extend the University of Arkansas’s leadership in contested logistics, military and defense logistics, and national security supply chains, in close partnership with the Contested Logistics Consortium and the Supply Chain Management Research Center (SCMRC). This cluster in contested logistics and supply chain aligns with one of the University’s and College’s key strategic priorities and builds critical mass in a high-importance academic and research domain. It advances the land-grant mission by connecting research, instruction, and outreach to pressing state and societal needs. This is a research-focused faculty position for a scholar with strong potential to publish high-impact, theoretically rigorous, and managerially relevant research in leading peer-reviewed supply chain management, logistics, operations, and business journals. The successful candidate will be expected to contribute to the department’s continued research excellence, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, engage meaningfully with students and doctoral candidates, and participate in service activities consistent with rank and career stage. The department is especially interested in candidates whose research addresses important supply chain challenges facing firms, industries, public institutions, and society. Areas of interest may include, but are not limited to resilience, risk, supply chain visibility, analytics, technology-enabled supply chains, defense and critical infrastructure supply chains, global networks, inventory and distribution systems, disruption management, and the interface between commercial and public-sector logistics systems. Consistent with the cluster hire strategy, the department has particular interest in candidates whose research directly addresses military logistics, contested logistics, and defense supply chain challenges, with opportunities to engage with the Contested Logistics Consortium and military and defense stakeholders. Candidates should demonstrate potential to produce research that is publishable in premier academic journals, with that research also generating insights that can inform industry practice, practitioner-oriented publications, executive audiences, and applied research partnerships. The position is aligned with the department’s broader commitment to academically excellent, industry-relevant scholarship and the Walton College’s distinctive access to leading companies, entrepreneurial ventures, public-sector partners, and supply chain innovators. Regular on-campus availability, in-person teaching, and active contribution to the life of the department, including exhibiting respect and cooperation in shared academic and administrative tasks are essential duties. Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: A completed Ph.D. in supply chain management, logistics, operations management, or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited business school or equivalent accredited institution completed by the position start date Demonstrated record or strong potential to publish research in top-tier supply chain management, logistics, operations, or business journals Evidence of research that has potential relevance for both academic journals and practitioner audiences Candidates must meet standards to be classified as a Scholarly Academic for AACSB purposes U.S. citizen, due to access to export-controlled information, restricted federal data, and security-sensitive research environments Preferred Qualifications: Strong research record and demonstrated leadership roles in research projects that result in top-tier journal publications Strong pipeline of research including manuscripts under second or third revision at top tier supply chain management journals Experience teaching courses related to logistics, procurement, transportation, operations, analytics, or supply chain strategy Research interests related to resilience and risk, supply chain visibility, analytics, robotics and automation, technology-enabled supply chains, defense and critical infrastructure supply chains, the interface between commercial and public-sector logistics systems, or other areas of strategic industry importance Industry work experience in supply chain management, logistics, operations, analytics, transportation, procurement, retail, manufacturing, defense, or related field An active U.S. security clearance, or eligibility to obtain and maintain one Significant military, defense logistics, or national security supply chain experience Knowledge, Skills and Abilities (KSAs): High-quality oral and written communication skills Ability to work collaboratively and collegially as a contributing member of a research-active faculty team Ability to engage with industry professionals, firms, public-sector organizations, or applied research partners Ability to teach in face-to-face, hybrid/blended, online, graduate, executive, or professional education formats Additional Information: This position is a Designated Research Position  and is regulated by the Arkansas Research Education Protection Act of 2025 .  Prior to issuance of an offer of employment, the University is required to request and obtain additional information about an applicant’s background and, if required, conduct an additional review of that background information. Salary Information: Commensurate with education and experience Required Documents to Apply: Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents: Proof of Veteran Status Recruitment Contact Information: Marc Scott Assistant Chair Sam M. Walton College of Business MScott@walton.uark.edu All application materials must be uploaded to the University of Arkansas System Career Site  https://uasys.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/UASYS   Please do not send to listed recruitment contact. Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Deadline is October 31, 2026 at 12:01 AM Pre-employment Screening Requirements: Criminal Background Check, Sex Offender Registry The University of Arkansas is committed to providing a safe campus community. We conduct background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and a sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check, a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check, and/or drug screening. Required checks are identified in the position listing. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. The University of Arkansas seeks to attract, develop and retain high quality faculty, staff and administrators that consistently display practices and behaviors to advance a culture that embeds equal opportunity, educational excellence and unparalleled access for all. The University of Arkansas is an equal opportunity institution. The University does not discriminate in its education programs or activities (including in admission and employment) on the basis of any category or status protected by law, including age, race, color, national origin, disability, religion, protected veteran status, military service, genetic information, sex, sexual preference, or pregnancy. Questions or concerns about the application of Title IX, which prohibits discrimination on the basis of sex, may be sent to the University’s Title IX Coordinator and to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Persons must have proof of legal authority to work in the United States on the first day of employment. All Application information is subject to public disclosure under the Arkansas Freedom of Information Act. Constant Physical Activity: N/A Frequent Physical Activity: N/A Occasional Physical Activity: N/A Benefits Eligible: Yes"
